    "done_when": "Done when an evidence record at docs/evidence/fragments/workers-spend-fewer-tokens-per-landed-node/interim-arm-report.html carries the per-arm table with intervals, the population sizes with every run listed by id (the wave's runs are the query's whole population), each arm's effort-hour mix, the draw's seed and assignment, the query that produced it, and the positive controls' results, and states that no verdict is drawn and that at this count the comparison is confounded by section. Negative control: the baseline local arm's runs are split into two halves of sizes as equal as the count allows, in every distinct way (three splits for four runs, ten for five), and the record reports the largest absolute value of those splits' differences in cumulative input per landed node, the statistic section 8's verdict rests on, as the spread a same-arm comparison already shows. No figure in the record is read as an arm difference, whatever its size: at this count neither a split difference nor an interval separates an arm's effect from the sections' difficulty, so the record gives each arm's figures beside that spread and calls no arm better or worse. A split whose half holds no landed node has no defined difference and is listed as undefined; if no split is defined the record states that the control could not be taken and why, and still reports each arm's figures. A resume, repair round or corrective redispatch of a wave run belongs to that run's node: its input is added to the node's total under the original run's arm, it is listed beside the original run's id, and it adds no run to the arm's count. An arm with no landed node reports its cumulative input per landed node as undefined, beside its run count and the input its runs spent. This section's node is dispatched only once every run of the wave has landed or been closed, so the record reads the whole population its done-when names.",
